# Security

Security is a first-class requirement.

Never:

- hardcode credentials
- commit secrets
- expose PostgreSQL publicly without a specific reason
- disable TLS in production
- disable certificate validation
- log passwords
- log access tokens
- log refresh tokens
- put secrets in source code

Use:

- environment variables
- secret managers in production
- HTTPS
- secure cookies
- short-lived access tokens
- appropriate refresh-token handling
- least privilege

Before changing authentication or authorization behavior,
consider the security impact.